      "rl.st.experiments.t7": "InSight lands in Elysium Planitia",
      "rl.st.experiments.t8": "Last communication from InSight",
      "rl.st.experiments.k1": "ALSEP stations", "rl.st.experiments.v1": "5 (Apollo 12, 14, 15, 16, 17)",
      "rl.st.experiments.k2": "ALSEP power", "rl.st.experiments.v2": "SNAP-27 radioisotope thermoelectric generator",
      "rl.st.experiments.k3": "Lunar laser reflectors in use", "rl.st.experiments.v3": "Apollo 11, 14, 15; Lunokhod 1 and 2",
      "rl.st.experiments.k4": "Marsquakes detected by InSight", "rl.st.experiments.v4": "more than 1,300",

      /* ---------- story 5 */
      "rl.st.descent.title": "The Final Descent",
      "rl.st.descent.tag": "How spacecraft reached the surface — and what their landing systems left behind",
      "rl.st.descent.lead": "Every object in this museum first had to survive a landing. The methods changed with each generation, and many landing systems still lie where they did their job.",
      "rl.st.descent.c1h": "Engines and legs",
      "rl.st.descent.c1": "Apollo lunar modules touched down on legs using their descent engines, and the Viking landers used throttled descent engines; on the Moon the descent stage then became the launch pad. Phoenix (2008) and InSight (2018) were also stationary landers on legs — InSight was built on Phoenix’s proven design.",
      "rl.st.descent.c2h": "Bouncing and lowering",
      "rl.st.descent.c2": "Mars Pathfinder (1997) landed inside airbags. Curiosity was too big and heavy for airbags, so in 2012 a rocket-powered sky crane lowered it on nylon ropes and then flew off to crash at a safe distance. Perseverance repeated the sky crane in 2021 and added terrain-relative navigation to steer to a safer spot.",
      "rl.st.descent.c3h": "Traces of a landing",
      "rl.st.descent.c3": "Orbital images often show the parachute, back shell and heat shield near a lander — for example at the Tianwen-1 / Zhurong site in 2021. In 2015 the same kind of images found Beagle 2, lost since 2003, with its solar panels only partly opened.",
